# EMAIL NOTIFICATION CONFIGURATION
# When a recipient accepts ("YES"), an email is automatically sent to the creator.
# You can configure either Resend (preferred) OR custom SMTP (Gmail, Outlook, SendGrid, etc.).
# If neither is set, the server uses Nodemailer Ethereal test inbox or logs to console.

# Option 1: Resend (Recommended, quick setup at https://resend.com)
RESEND_API_KEY=""

# Option 2: Custom SMTP (e.g., Gmail with App Password, SendGrid, Postmark, AWS SES)
# SMTP_HOST="smtp.gmail.com"
# SMTP_PORT="587"
# SMTP_SECURE="false"
# SMTP_USER="your-email@gmail.com"
# SMTP_PASS="your-app-specific-password"
# SMTP_FROM="Will You Be My Girlfriend? <noreply@yourdomain.com>"

# DATABASE PERSISTENCE ON VERCEL (Optional)
# By default, invitations are saved in memory and backed by atomic disk storage (/tmp in serverless).
# To enable multi-region, persistent cloud storage across all Vercel cold starts,
# connect an Upstash Redis or Vercel KV store (1-click in Vercel Integrations):
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=""
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=""
# Or Vercel KV:
# KV_REST_API_URL=""
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=""
